{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan an Nasai","section":{"13":{"eng-name":"The Book of Forgetfulness (In Prayer)","ara-name":"كتاب السهو"}},"section_detail":{"13":{"hadithnumber_first":1179,"hadithnumber_last":1366,"arabicnumber_first":1179,"arabicnumber_last":1366}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":1212,"arabicnumber":1212,"text":"Rapporté par ‘Ali : J’avais deux moments où j’entrais chez le Messager d’Allah (ﷺ), un la nuit et un pendant la journée. Quand j’entrais la nuit, il toussait légèrement pour m’indiquer que je pouvais entrer","grades":[{"name":"Abu Ghuddah","grade":"Daif Isnaad"},{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Daif Isnaad"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}],"reference":{"book":13,"hadith":34},"chapter":{"id":17,"ara-name":"باب التَّنَحْنُحِ فِي الصَّلاَةِ","eng-name":"Clearing the throat while praying","isFirstHadith":false}}]}